{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvQM7GpP15cLGDwTSYxp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing in the design files would change how the comparison is read. In `samples.csv` and `rnaseq_bulk_design.csv`, `condition` and `group` are identical: S1–S3 are control and S4–S6 are treated, with replicates 1–3 in each. That gives a simple two-group comparison with 3 vs 3 samples and no other recorded factor, such as batch, donor/pairing or sequencing lane.\n\nOne caveat: those files can only show what you entered. If anything else differs between the two conditions, like processing day, library prep batch or source animal, the design can't separate it from the treatment. Any difference found would then be blamed on treatment. Three replicates per arm also limits power to detect small changes. The source directory contained a non-FASTQ file, `README_runsheet.txt`. It was excluded at registration, and I haven't read it because it's outside what these stages may read. If it records run or batch details, it's worth checking yourself for that kind of confound.\n\nPending: say when you're ready and I'll start the bioinformatics for rnaseq_bulk."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":50065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b4243e3-d471-5e71-aa05-ba99b39a8e9a","uuid":"aae662d0-5026-453c-b0a5-97d17de7fc49","timestamp":"2026-11-11T03:07:37.913Z","request_id":"req_011CgvQM75uPPqNMPBbnNbTP"}
